00:19:02.274 --> 00:19:05.878 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I personally respect
religious liberty,

00:19:05.878 --> 00:19:08.947
as long as it does not step
on my individual liberty.

00:19:08.947 --> 00:19:12.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know that some religious
conservatives don't love that,

00:19:13.085 --> 00:19:15.220
and there's reasons for that.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.022
But that's the stuff
we have to hash out.

00:19:17.022 --> 00:19:18.924
That's worthy of hashing out.

00:19:18.924 --> 00:19:21.660 align:start position:0%
Because the alternative Michael
is at the end of the day,

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.595
if we don't do this
thing, they won.

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:25.063
- We get run over.

00:19:25.063 --> 00:19:26.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
- They won, it's over,
- We get run over.

00:19:26.565 --> 00:19:28.700
- congratulations, we're
all in the gulag together.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.335 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then we're gonna really
have to live together

00:19:30.335 --> 00:19:32.337
in small cells, and eat gruel,

00:19:32.337 --> 00:19:34.039
and it's very cold
and wet in there.

00:19:34.039 --> 00:19:37.242
And I don't know that I wanna
be in there with you frankly.

00:19:37.242 --> 00:19:39.411
- Well, so since
you bring it up,

00:19:39.411 --> 00:19:41.280
you bring up this word sanctity.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:44.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
You bring up sort of
these religious questions.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.719 align:start size:84% position:16%
You mention we've
gotta hash this out.

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:51.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Cardinal Manning famously
said, all politics,

00:19:51.456 --> 00:19:54.393
all human conflict basically
is theological at the bottom.

00:19:54.393 --> 00:19:58.363
One of the more striking
points in your book is,

00:19:59.565 --> 00:20:01.700
when we first met
each other, Dave,

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
when we first became
pals, you were an atheist.

00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:06.471
- Yeah.

00:20:06.471 --> 00:20:10.442
- Today you are not
exactly an atheist.

00:20:10.442 --> 00:20:12.878
- No, I am a believer.

00:20:12.878 --> 00:20:13.712
- You're a believer.
- There is no question

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:14.947
about it.

00:20:14.947 --> 00:20:16.915 line:0%
I am willing to
say that Knowles.

00:20:16.915 --> 00:20:19.251 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Yeah.
- How did it happen?

00:20:19.251 --> 00:20:21.286 line:0%
- Look, there were
a couple of things.

00:20:21.286 --> 00:20:24.890
Partly one of the reasons,
I had never, as an adult,

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:28.493
I had never said I was an
atheist until about 2000.

00:20:28.493 --> 00:20:30.729 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think it was, if I
remember exactly correctly,

00:20:30.729 --> 00:20:33.699
it was the fall of 2015.

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:37.469 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I am now in 2022,
I'm 45-years-old.

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:40.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
So this is about seven years
ago, I'm in my late 30s.

00:20:40.872 --> 00:20:44.276
And I always sort of
felt somewhat agnostic,

00:20:44.276 --> 00:20:45.944
but I always love
logic and reason.

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:48.280
I grew up reading all
of Carl Sagan's books.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.382
So I loved sort of,

00:20:50.382 --> 00:20:53.385 align:start size:97% position:3%
I loved sort of a distant
respect for belief in a way,

00:20:53.385 --> 00:20:57.189 align:start size:97% position:3%
but not like a hardcore
belief, something like that.

00:20:57.189 --> 00:20:59.658 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, I also, I come
from a secular Jewish family

00:20:59.658 --> 00:21:02.828 align:start size:97% position:3%
that while we did all of
the holidays and traditions,

00:21:02.828 --> 00:21:06.531
which is basically what kept
Jews around for 5,000 years,

00:21:06.531 --> 00:21:08.267
it's different in terms of,

00:21:08.267 --> 00:21:11.036
the belief in God is
a little bit different

00:21:11.036 --> 00:21:13.238
than say a Catholic, or-

00:21:13.238 --> 00:21:17.209 align:start size:88% position:13%
- We like to say secular
Judaism is Jew-ish.

00:21:17.209 --> 00:21:19.077
You know, emphasis on the ish.

00:21:19.077 --> 00:21:21.113
- Yeah, and by the way, our
good friend Dennis Prager

00:21:21.113 --> 00:21:22.648
has written many
books about this.

00:21:22.648 --> 00:21:24.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
That maybe that thing
just can't last that long,

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.319 align:start size:97% position:3%
that it's not enough to
like Seinfeld and eat bagels

00:21:27.319 --> 00:21:31.123 align:start size:84% position:16%
and all of those
things, although those
are worthy things.

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:35.394 align:start size:97% position:3%
Man, I made an everything
bagel at Locs the other day,

00:21:35.394 --> 00:21:36.662
Miami, you can get a,

00:21:36.662 --> 00:21:38.263
they say it's all in
New York and Jersey.

00:21:38.263 --> 00:21:39.598
I know you're a New
Yorker originally.

00:21:39.598 --> 00:21:41.033
- Yes.

00:21:41.033 --> 00:21:41.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
- You can get a good
bagel down here in Miami.

00:21:41.867 --> 00:21:43.135
But putting that aside-

00:21:43.135 --> 00:21:44.670 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well because where did
the New York Jews go?

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.204
They've all fled now, right?

00:21:46.204 --> 00:21:48.006
They're all heading down to
the free state of Florida.

00:21:48.006 --> 00:21:50.075
- All the sane ones
now are in Florida,

00:21:50.075 --> 00:21:52.477
and it's just the bananas
ones still in New York.

00:21:52.477 --> 00:21:55.180
But in any essence, in 2015,

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.716 align:start position:0%
I started having a bunch of
well known atheists on my show.

00:21:57.716 --> 00:22:00.585
Primarily Sam Harris was
sort of the first one.

00:22:00.585 --> 00:22:03.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just sort of started
going into that world.

00:22:03.889 --> 00:22:06.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
And for a long time, I
never said I was an atheist,

00:22:06.725 --> 00:22:09.061
but a lot of people just kept
saying, Dave's an atheist,

00:22:09.061 --> 00:22:11.663
because it was just by the
nature of the conversations

00:22:11.663 --> 00:22:12.864
that I was having.

00:22:12.864 --> 00:22:14.399
I had Ayaan Hirsi Ali on,

00:22:14.399 --> 00:22:17.703
and Pete Bogosian who wrote a
manual for creating atheists.

00:22:17.703 --> 00:22:19.471 align:start size:88% position:13%
And Michael Shermer
from "Skeptic Magazine".

00:22:19.471 --> 00:22:20.605
I know you know all these guys.

00:22:20.605 --> 00:22:22.174 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah.
- And so I just sort of

00:22:22.174 --> 00:22:24.609 align:start size:88% position:13%
got in, like sort of
caught up in that thing.

00:22:24.609 --> 00:22:27.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
But then eventually I started
saying I was an atheist.

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.848
I would say a couple things
started moving me on this.

00:22:29.848 --> 00:22:31.516
First off, as you know,
a couple of years later,

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:32.951 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was on tour with
Jordan Peterson

00:22:32.951 --> 00:22:35.887 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we did 120 shows
in 20 countries.

00:22:35.887 --> 00:22:39.725
And he was not only, I had
read "12 Rules for Life"

00:22:39.725 --> 00:22:41.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had flipped through
"Maps of Meaning",

00:22:41.626 --> 00:22:45.330
it's a very intense book, but
being on tour with this guy

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:48.333 align:start size:88% position:13%
and every night hearing
a different speech

00:22:48.333 --> 00:22:52.304
related to the importance of
belief, and that in many ways,

00:22:52.304 --> 00:22:56.408
whether you believe you are
or not, you are a believer.

00:22:56.408 --> 00:22:59.244 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I don't mean this to attack
Sam Harris, for example,

00:22:59.244 --> 00:23:01.446
but Sam Harris says he's not
a believer, he's an atheist.

00:23:01.446 --> 00:23:04.249 align:start size:97% position:3%
But it's like he does believe
that Trump is the devil.

00:23:04.249 --> 00:23:05.784
That's where all of his actions

00:23:05.784 --> 00:23:07.986
over the last couple of years
politically seem to come from.

00:23:07.986 --> 00:23:09.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't really mean that-
- Wow,

00:23:09.254 --> 00:23:10.422
he might not believe in God,

00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:11.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
but he does believe
in the devil.

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:13.525
That's a great observation.

00:23:13.525 --> 00:23:16.027
- I get one, one a show,
that's what I always say.

00:23:17.729 --> 00:23:20.298 align:start size:97% position:3%
Then I heard Jordan say a
few things related to belief

00:23:20.298 --> 00:23:22.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
specifically that I
really loved, one of them,

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.635
you may have heard this.

00:23:23.635 --> 00:23:25.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was on, this is a
little bit later actually.

00:23:25.237 --> 00:23:27.005
So I'm jumping ahead a bit.

00:23:27.005 --> 00:23:29.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was on Tucker
Carlson's Fox Nation show,

00:23:29.441 --> 00:23:31.743 align:start size:88% position:13%
and he was talking about
the nature of belief.

00:23:31.743 --> 00:23:33.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he said that when
he was in his early 20s,

00:23:33.745 --> 00:23:36.448
he decided to tell the truth

00:23:36.448 --> 00:23:38.350 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the sake of
telling the truth.

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:40.585
That in essence, that
if you told the truth,

00:23:40.585 --> 00:23:43.188
that that would be the best
outcome, no matter what.

00:23:43.188 --> 00:23:44.956 align:start size:88% position:13%
Doesn't mean that it
would be a good outcome,

00:23:44.956 --> 00:23:46.291
because obviously you
can tell the truth

00:23:46.291 --> 00:23:48.026
and they might hang you for it.

00:23:48.026 --> 00:23:50.729
But actually it would
be the best outcome.

00:23:50.729 --> 00:23:52.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's an incredible
leap of faith.

00:23:52.397 --> 00:23:54.466
To believe in truth
for truth's sake,

00:23:54.466 --> 00:23:56.968 align:start size:88% position:13%
there's no tangible
reason to believe that.

00:23:56.968 --> 00:23:58.770
In many cases there's
the reverse of that,

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:01.006 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we know what happens
to truth tellers, right?

00:24:01.006 --> 00:24:03.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're gonna be
lambasted, and ask Jesus,

00:24:03.708 --> 00:24:04.943
there's a lot of things

00:24:04.943 --> 00:24:06.745
that are bad that are
gonna happen, right.

00:24:06.745 --> 00:24:08.980
But I really love that
explanation of truth.

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:12.918
That truth for truth's
sake is a leap of faith

00:24:12.918 --> 00:24:14.386
in and of itself.

00:24:14.386 --> 00:24:16.621
What a great kernel that
is to start with something.

00:24:16.621 --> 00:24:20.926
And then through the year of
hearing Jordan talk about this,

00:24:20.926 --> 00:24:25.030 align:start size:97% position:3%
and really also it wasn't just
at a personal level for me,

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:27.632
because I do the politics
thing that you do as well.

00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:31.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
I talk about things broadly
at a societal level,

00:24:31.603 --> 00:24:35.106
and it's like, it's not
working without belief.

00:24:35.106 --> 00:24:38.343
Once you remove God, Nietzsche
said, you know, God is dead,

00:24:38.343 --> 00:24:41.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that's a warning
to you people.

00:24:41.112 --> 00:24:42.380
People think, oh God's dead,

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:43.815
let's do whatever
the hell we want.

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:45.183 align:start size:97% position:3%
But it's actually a warning
'cause it's like man,

00:24:45.183 --> 00:24:46.651
that hole is big.

00:24:46.651 --> 00:24:48.153
That hole is big and
you're gonna fill it

00:24:48.153 --> 00:24:49.788
with some other crazy shit.

00:24:49.788 --> 00:24:51.890
And congratulations,
now boys are girls,

00:24:51.890 --> 00:24:55.126
non-racist are racists,
two plus two is five.

00:24:55.126 --> 00:24:56.628
The litany of Latinx

00:24:56.628 --> 00:24:59.564 align:start size:97% position:3%
and all the other nonsensical
phrases that we have,

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:02.000
that's what we filled it with.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.302 align:start size:88% position:13%
We filled it with
secularism on steroids.

00:25:04.302 --> 00:25:06.838
It's not to say that secularism,

00:25:06.838 --> 00:25:10.842
and your ability to live as
you wish, is not important.

00:25:10.842 --> 00:25:12.344
Of course it's important.

00:25:12.344 --> 00:25:16.381
And I wanna live in a largely
secular society obviously.

00:25:16.381 --> 00:25:18.650
But we need some
guardrails on that.

00:25:18.650 --> 00:25:22.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would say, some
people's belief is purely,

00:25:22.487 --> 00:25:24.389
it's purely spiritual.

00:25:24.389 --> 00:25:29.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
They feel a very deep
spiritual sense of belief.

00:25:30.829 --> 00:25:32.097
I wouldn't say that's the
primary driver of mine.

00:25:32.097 --> 00:25:36.334
I would say it's a
logical, rational,

00:25:36.334 --> 00:25:39.104
and almost necessary need
for belief, I would say.

00:25:40.205 --> 00:25:41.973
But I certainly feel it more.

00:25:41.973 --> 00:25:44.009
Maybe it's a little
bit, I'm 45 now,

00:25:44.009 --> 00:25:46.645
so this is definitely what I
suppose they call middle age.

00:25:46.645 --> 00:25:48.246
You young whippersnapper!

00:25:48.246 --> 00:25:49.714
And so maybe it's a
little bit of that.

00:25:49.714 --> 00:25:51.483
Maybe it's also, it
was one of the things

00:25:51.483 --> 00:25:53.585
that made me wanna
finally have kids

00:25:53.585 --> 00:25:55.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
after not wanting to have
kids for a long time.

00:25:57.322 --> 00:25:59.157 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's something going on
here that's beyond us Knowles,

00:25:59.157 --> 00:26:02.260 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I think societies
have to understand that.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:06.798
Otherwise the winds of
the day will blow over

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:07.999
the whole thing every time.

00:26:07.999 --> 00:26:10.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
We are in the middle
of it right now.

00:26:10.502 --> 00:26:12.003
- It's a similar thing-

00:26:12.003 --> 00:26:13.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I like you there, I feel
pretty good about that.

00:26:13.505 --> 00:26:16.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, no it, I think
you're pretty close to it.

00:26:17.709 --> 00:26:21.179
What you're really
close to here is,

00:26:21.179 --> 00:26:24.716
is something that so
many people on the left

00:26:24.716 --> 00:26:29.321
refuse to get to,
which is humility.

00:26:29.321 --> 00:26:31.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just saying, there's
something bigger than me.

00:26:31.389 --> 00:26:32.924
Maybe I don't have
all the answers.

00:26:32.924 --> 00:26:34.693
Maybe I need to suppress

00:26:34.693 --> 00:26:37.262 align:start size:84% position:16%
at least some of my
interests and desires,

00:26:37.262 --> 00:26:39.064
for the truth for truth's sake.

00:26:39.064 --> 00:26:42.200 align:start size:84% position:16%
Similar thing
happened to me with,

00:26:42.200 --> 00:26:43.802
I was an atheist for 10 years,

00:26:43.802 --> 00:26:46.471
and I was pretty
hardcore about it.

00:26:46.471 --> 00:26:49.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was pretty firmly atheistic
for most of that time.

00:26:49.507 --> 00:26:54.245
And it was only an
intellectual journey.

00:26:54.245 --> 00:26:58.617
It was only just reading
and logic and arguments

00:26:58.617 --> 00:27:00.151
that took me from,

00:27:01.519 --> 00:27:02.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
at least that's how it
appeared to me at the time,

00:27:02.954 --> 00:27:06.024 align:start size:97% position:3%
to go from atheist, to
being open to that question.

00:27:06.024 --> 00:27:07.926
Now I would say there was
a little more spiritually

00:27:07.926 --> 00:27:09.160
going on too.

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:10.495 align:start size:81% position:19%
But it was only
after all of that,

00:27:10.495 --> 00:27:12.430
that I started to have
really what you'd call

00:27:12.430 --> 00:27:13.965
religious or spiritual feeling.

00:27:13.965 --> 00:27:17.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as you describe
Dave, the more you do it,

00:27:17.035 --> 00:27:19.471
the more you do it, the
more it happens to you,

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:21.740
the more you practice
these kinds of things.

00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:25.910
And so it, this raises then
a question for the book,

00:27:25.910 --> 00:27:27.812
and we're joking about
what your next book is.

00:27:27.812 --> 00:27:29.214
We joke about how
you're gonna end up

00:27:29.214 --> 00:27:30.715
to the right of Mussolini,

00:27:30.715 --> 00:27:32.684
and all of us are gonna say
Dave, what are you doing,

00:27:32.684 --> 00:27:34.285
you gotta come further left.

00:27:34.285 --> 00:27:37.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
But a lot of times people
who are on the left,

00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:40.325
who then move in more
conservative circles,

00:27:40.325 --> 00:27:43.662
they say, I didn't leave
my party, my party left me.

00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:45.897
And Bill Maher just came
out and said this again.

00:27:45.897 --> 00:27:48.633
And certainly that
happens sometimes.

00:27:48.633 --> 00:27:51.002
But it seems to me,
reading your book,

00:27:51.002 --> 00:27:53.004 align:start size:88% position:13%
